0..72 Comment "/// This source states the words of two spherical cells at one point, at"
73..114 Comment "/// dimension two and at dimension three."
115..118 Comment "///"
119..196 Comment "/// A spherical cell is central, so the words of spherical cells commute. Two"
197..271 Comment "/// words that differ by the order of their letters are one word. A letter"
272..350 Comment "/// cancels its inverse at any distance. Two words that differ by a count stay"
351..400 Comment "/// apart. Loops at dimension one do not commute."
401..404 Comment "///"
405..478 Comment "/// The checker and the kernel bring each word above dimension one to one"
479..553 Comment "/// normal form: the letters sorted by their cells, and each cell counted."
554..557 Comment "///"
558..632 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/sphere.gandr — one cell for each sphere"
633..704 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/circle.gandr — the words of one loop"
